\title{Tasks and evaluation interfaces}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{notes}

\p{A model does not have a benchmark score without a task distribution, an
inference procedure, and an evaluator. Keeping these objects separate is
essential for post-training: a training change and an evaluation-time search
change can raise the same reported score while answering different research
questions.}

